Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Disables Edge sign-in and sync entirely. This is the policy that makes the rest of the
; MSA-scoped tweaks in this folder (TrackingPrevention, SyncDisabled, EdgeCopilotEnabled,
; and friends) actually apply - Microsoft: "Starting in Microsoft Edge version 116, certain
; policies will not be applied to a profile that is signed in with a Microsoft account."
; Cost: no favorites/password/tab sync, no Microsoft Rewards, no website SSO from this
; profile. Delete this file to keep sign-in and sync - most of the other Edge tweaks in
; this folder go quiet the moment you sign back in, so deleting it isn't free.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge]
"BrowserSignin"=dword:00000000
"SyncDisabled"=dword:00000001

; Required alongside BrowserSignin=0 - Microsoft's own doc for NonRemovableProfileEnabled
; says so explicitly, since that policy otherwise creates an automatically signed-in
; browser profile. ImplicitSignInEnabled is deliberately left out: its own doc says it
; "doesn't take any effect" once BrowserSignin is set to Disable.
"NonRemovableProfileEnabled"=dword:00000000
